<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="list_items.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="list_items">
    <!-- P3 track-A: the nearby-items list (game::list_items, the `V` screen).
         A right-docked panel mirroring list_monsters: a header (<Tab> Items +
         the active/total counter), a scrolling list of nearby item stacks
         (magenta category headers — sort-by-category mode — interspersed with
         item rows: a coloured name on the left, an optional NEW! badge, and a
         distance/direction cluster on the right), the selected stack's info pane
         (rml_util::item_info_rml_lines — the shared item-info producer), and a
         footer hint line. Render-only: the keyboard owns cursor nav / filter /
         priority / examine / compare / travel; the doc is synced each frame from
         filtered_items/iActive. The curses calcStartPos windowing is dropped for
         native scroll (selected row scrolled into view on move). Per-segment
         colour (priority yellow/red, in-inventory colour, NEW! green) is baked
         via cata_text_to_rml. -->
    <div class="panel li-panel">
        <div class="li-header" data-rml="header_rml"></div>
        <div id="li-list" class="li-list scroll-pane">
            <div data-if="empty" class="li-empty" data-rml="empty_rml"></div>
            <div class="li-row" data-for="r : rows" data-class-selected="r.selected"
                 data-class-cat="r.is_cat">
                <span class="li-cat" data-if="r.is_cat" data-rml="r.cat_rml"></span>
                <span class="li-name" data-if="!r.is_cat" data-rml="r.name_rml"></span>
                <span class="li-new" data-if="r.has_new" data-rml="r.new_rml"></span>
                <span class="li-dist" data-if="!r.is_cat" data-rml="r.dist_rml"></span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="li-info-title" data-rml="info_title_rml"></div>
        <div id="li-info" class="li-info scroll-pane">
            <div class="li-info-line" data-for="ln : info" data-rml="ln.text_rml"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="li-footer" data-rml="footer_rml"></div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
